    "result_text": "All tests pass (BUILD SUCCESS). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a `bulkSignupWarning` flag to owner responses: `true` when more than 80 owners have already been registered on the current date, otherwise `false`. It appears on both the create response (`POST /api/owners`) and the read response (`GET /api/owners/{ownerId}`), which is what the acceptance test exercises.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection pattern, I kept each piece of logic in its own single-responsibility unit:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so `OwnerDto` is regenerated with the field.\n- **`ResolveBulkSignupWarning`** (new function) \u2014 the only place the rule lives: counts owners registered on the current date via the existing `OwnerRepository.countByRegistrationDate`, and publishes `Out<Boolean>` when the count exceeds the threshold (80). It reuses the same per-day accumulation path as `EnsureDailyOwnerLimit` and follows the existing `Resolve*` naming (cf. `ResolveRegistrationDate`).\n- **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 a small `toOwnerDto(Owner, boolean)` overload that delegates to the existing mapping and attaches the response-only flag, so the attach logic lives once rather than being duplicated per responder.\n- **`RespondWithOwner`** and **`RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 each now reads `@Val Boolean bulkSignupWarning` and passes it to the mapper.\n- **YAML pipelines** \u2014 wired a `resolveBulkWarning` step before `respond` in both `owners.POST.yml` (`govern: [ transaction ]`) and `owners/{ownerId}.GET.yml` (`govern: [ readonly-transaction ]`).\n\n`PUT` and list/page responses were intentionally left untouched \u2014 the requirement scopes the warning to the create/read flow, and the single-arg mapper method keeps those paths unchanged.",
